Approach: Use sliding window allowing at most one zero. Expand right, and shrink from left when zeros exceed one, tracking maximum window size (excluding one element).

Time Complexity: O(n) — each element is processed at most twice by the pointers.

Space Complexity: O(1) — only variables used, no extra space.
class Solution {
    public int longestSubarray(int[] arr) {
        int left=0,right=0,n=arr.length,count=0,maxlen=0;
        while(right<n){
            if(arr[right]==0){
                count++;
            }
            while(count>1){
                if(arr[left]==0){
                    count--;
                }
                left++;
            }
            if(count<=1){
                maxlen=Math.max(maxlen,right-left);
            }
            right++;
        }
        return maxlen;
    }
}
